<article class="env-lemma" id="0BFW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BFW">Lemma <span data-tag="0BFW">54.6.2</span>.</a> Let $S, s_ i, S_ i$ be as in (<a href="/tag/0BFU" data-tag="0BFU">54.6.0.1</a>). If $f : X \to S$ corresponds to $g_ i : Y_ i \to S_ i$ under $F$, then $f$ is separated, proper, finite, if and only if $g_ i$ is so for $i = 1, \ldots , n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Limits, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BFN" data-tag="0BFN">32.21.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>